    "https://www.sfu.ca/vpacademic/our-role/academic-planning/enrolment-class-composition.html": {
      "title": "Enrollment & Class Composition",
      "description": "Enrollment & Class Composition - Provost and VP Academic - Simon Fraser University Skip to content Skip to main navigation sfu.ca Faculty & Staff Forms MENU undefined undefined Provost and VP Academic Sign In SFU Mail go SFU Canvas Search undefined This Site SFU.ca Who We Are About Provost's Office Meet the Provost Meet The Team Committees Our Role Academic Planning Resource Planning Budget Office Support Services Institutional Initiatives Awards Distinguished SFU Professors Excellence in Teaching Nora and Ted Sterling Prize Academic Careers Current Openings Administrative Appointments Academic Positions Current Research Chair Opportunities News Faculty & Staff Forms Overview Provost and VP Academic Our Role Academic Planning Enrollment & Class Composition Provost and VP Academic Who We Are About Provost's Office Meet the Provost Meet The Team Committees Our Role Academic Planning Academic Planning Accreditation External Reviews Curriculum Development General Education (WQB) Requirements Program Development General Education (WQB) Certification Resources Faculty Renewal Enrollment & Class Composition Educational Goals Program-level Educational Goals Institutional Educational Goals Institutional Accountability Resource Planning Finance & Budgeting Space Management Budget Office Current Year Next Year Tuition Setting Budget FAQ's Support Services Learning & Teaching Institutional Initiatives Awards Distinguished SFU Professors Excellence in Teaching SFU Gallery of Teaching Excellence SFU Teaching Awards Nora and Ted Sterling Prize Academic Careers Current Openings Administrative Appointments Academic Positions Current Research Chair Opportunities Canada Impact+ Research Chairs News Faculty & Staff Forms Overview New Faculty Start-Up Grants and Faculty Recruitment Grants New Continuing Staff Requests Enrollment & Class Composition Our students are central to realizing SFU’s vision as Canada’s leading engaged university. Enrollment Management Strategic enrollment management considers a complex set of policies and practices that impact the size and composition of our student body, including recruitment, admission, and registration of new students; success and retention of existing students; student credit-loads; and the number of students completing programs. Strategic enrollment planning establishes multi-year goals for these variables and guides enrollment decisions over time as we deliver a welcoming and inclusive student experience and exceptional academic programming that meets diverse student needs. SFU Long-range Strategic Enrollment Plan In 2020, SFU initiated a new strategic enrollment planning model, building on the longstanding work of the undergraduate Strategic Enrollment Management Council and the Senate Committee on Enrollment Management and Planning. The Strategic Enrollment Planning Committee (SEPC) was created to coordinate the efforts of strategic enrollment management committees focused on undergraduate (SEMC-UG), graduate (SEMC-GS), and non-credit (SEMC-NC) studies with representation from all Faculties, Graduate Studies, Lifelong Learning, and the Office of the Registrar and Student Enrollment. Through the work of these committees and consultation, the Long-Range Strategic Enrollment Plan was introduced in 2021. This plan expanded prior enrollment planning work largely focused on undergraduate studies and established a set of Strategic Enrollment Planning Guidelines as a framework for calibrating enrollments over a multi-year planning horizon. Originally intended to set five-year goals, the timeline has since been extended to six years due to the significant impact of the pandemic on enrollments. Find Out More Learn more about the SFU Long-Range Strategic Enrollment Plan (2021-2027). Share the plan in your unit as context for strategic enrollment management activities. Send questions about the plan to avpacad@sfu.ca . LONG-RANGE STRATEGIC ENROLLMENT PLANNING MODEL: COMMITTEE STRUCTURE AND CONSULTATION Provost and VP Academic Who We Are Our Role Awards Academic Careers News Faculty & Staff Forms Contact us 8888 University Drive Burnaby, B.C. Canada V5A 1S6 Safety & Risk SFU Maps & Directions SFU Admissions Road Report Give to SFU Emergency Information A-Z Directory Simon Fraser University respectfully acknowledges the xʷməθkʷəy̓əm (Musqueam), Sḵwx̱wú7mesh Úxwumixw (Squamish), səlilwətaɬ (Tsleil-Waututh), q̓íc̓əy̓ (Katzie), kʷikʷəƛ̓əm (Kwikwetlem), Qayqayt, Kwantlen, Semiahmoo and Tsawwassen peoples on whose unceded traditional territories our three campuses reside. Terms & Conditions Privacy policy © Simon Fraser University Provost and VP Academic Who We Are Overview About Provost's Office Meet the Provost Meet The Team Committees Our Role Overview Academic Planning Overview Academic Planning Accreditation External Reviews Curriculum Development General Education (WQB) Requirements Program Development General Education (WQB) Certification Resources Faculty Renewal Enrollment & Class Composition Educational Goals Program-level Educational Goals Institutional Educational Goals Institutional Accountability Resource Planning Overview Finance & Budgeting Space Management Budget Office Overview Current Year Next Year Tuition Setting Budget FAQ's Support Services Overview Learning & Teaching Institutional Initiatives Awards Overview Distinguished SFU Professors Excellence in Teaching Overview SFU Gallery of Teaching Excellence SFU Teaching Awards Nora and Ted Sterling Prize Academic Careers Overview Current Openings Administrative Appointments Academic Positions Current Research Chair Opportunities Overview Canada Impact+ Research Chairs News Faculty & Staff Forms Overview Overview Overview New Faculty Start-Up Grants and Faculty Recruitment Grants New Continuing Staff Requests Faculty & Staff Forms SFU.CA Search Search undefined This Site SFU.ca SFU Mail go SFU Canvas close"
